================================================================================
Third-party references
================================================================================

This is a clean-room reimplementation of the Sigma fp L tethering protocol,
derived from publicly observable USB PTP traffic against a Sigma fp L camera
and cross-referenced against the following open-source projects.

NO PROPRIETARY SIGMA SDK SOURCE CODE OR HEADERS ARE INCLUDED OR REQUIRED.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* libgphoto2  (https://github.com/gphoto/libgphoto2)

  GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.

  We used libgphoto2 as a protocol reference implementation. Specifically,
  the file `camlibs/ptp2/ptp.h` documents PTP vendor opcodes — many of which
  are protocol facts observable in any USB capture of a Sigma camera. Where
  our `fp_l_tether/camera/ptp_codes.py` lists Sigma vendor opcodes, those
  values are also present in libgphoto2's `ptp.h` and have been observed
  by us in live USB traffic from a Sigma fp L.

  libgphoto2 maintainers (notably Marcus Meissner) reverse-engineered Sigma
  camera behaviour by working directly with the hardware. We have NOT
  copied any source code from libgphoto2 into this project; we re-implemented
  the protocol behaviour in Python from observation.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* sigma-ptpy  (https://github.com/makanikai/sigma-ptpy)

  Independent Python implementation of the Sigma PTP protocol by makanikai.
  We cross-referenced our DataGroup FieldPresent bitmask observations against
  sigma-ptpy's published schema and found them consistent with the wire data
  produced by our own Sigma fp L. We have NOT imported or vendored any code
  from sigma-ptpy.

